export const str REGISTRY_SRC =
    "# CobaltC Diagnostic Registry\n\nStatus: normative artifact\nVersion: 1.61.0\nConforms to: `spec/02-sche"
    "ma.md` (Kind: Diagnostic, `diag.<name>`)\nGoverned by: `CobaltC_Master_Instructions.md` §19\n\n## Purp"
    "ose\n\nEvery `diag.*` id any rule produces, with the fields §19 requires.\nEvery entry has **Status:**"
    " ACCEPTED. Conventions: **Phase** is\n*static* (a `disposition: rejected` rule, or a `checked` rule w"
    "hose\nguard `rule.control.flow-analysis` refuted), *dynamic* (a `checked`\nrule's runtime guard), or *"
    "both*. **Summary** is the diagnostic's\nmessage when its occurrence gives none of its own. **Location"
    "** is,\nunless stated, the expression the triggering rule's premises were\nevaluated against; it is a "
    "file, a line and a column, the column being\nthat of the location's first token, counted in character"
    "s from 1 (a\nlocation that is a declaration or a statement is its first token).\n**Related** cites `ex"
    ".*` (`spec/examples.md`). When a program has\nseveral static errors, the one reported is the first in"
    " the source (the\nlowest line; among one line's errors, any), whatever order a checker\nvisits the pro"
    "gram in (`CHG-0130`).\n\n**How a diagnostic is shown** (D-0228). Both implementations print every\ndiag"
    "nostic in the same form, byte for byte. By default it is short: a first\nline `error[diag.x]: message"
    "` for a static diagnostic or `fault[diag.x]:\nmessage` for a dynamic one, where the message is the oc"
    "currence's own or\nthe entry's **Summary**; then `--> file:line:column`; then the source line,\nread f"
    "rom the file when the diagnostic is shown, with carets under the\nlocation's token; then `= repair:` "
    "and the entry's **Repair**. A file\nthat cannot be read is shown as its location alone. With `--expla"
    "in`\n(both tools), or with `COBALTC_EXPLAIN` set to anything but empty or `0`\n(this is how a compiled"
    " program is asked), the entry's Rule, Invariant,\nRequired, Observed and Provenance follow, then its "
    "Related examples and\nthis registry. A conformance case requires the id and the phase\n(`spec/conforma"
    "nce.md`), which a runner reads from the first line's\nopening `error[diag.ID]` or `fault[diag.ID]` (`"
    "impl/conformance/run.py`);\nthe location is as this registry gives it; the rest of the form's\nwording"
    " is not normative.\n\n## Syntax\n\n- `diag.syntax-error` — Summary: the text is not a CobaltC program "
    "here. Phase: static. Rule: the grammar, `spec/22` (lexical §1, syntactic §2–§3, and each rule t"
    "hat makes a form a syntax error, such as `[Slice-Not-Borrowed]`). Invariant: none. Required: the tex"
    "t is a CobaltC program by the grammar. Observed: at the location, the first token (or character) whe"
    "re the grammar allows none of what the message says was expected; nothing of the program runs. Prove"
    "nance: the source text. Repair: correct the text there; the message names what was expected and what"
    " was found. Location: that token.\n\n## Names and scoping\n\n- `diag.unbound-name` — Summary: this nam"
    "e is not declared. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.value-object.binding-lookup` `[Binding-Lookup-Unbound]"
    "`, `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Unbound]`, `spec/21` §0 `fault`'s name (D-0083). Invariant: none"
    ". Required: the name resolves to a binding or item. Observed: it does not. Provenance: use site vs. "
    "every declaration in scope. Repair: declare it, fix the spelling, or add an `import` (`import std;` "
    "for the standard library, `CHG-0033`). Related: `ex.unbound-name`.\n- `diag.ambiguous-name` — Summa"
    "ry: this name could mean more than one item. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Am"
    "biguous]`. Required: exactly one candidate. Observed: several (two `import`s, two imported modules e"
    "xporting the name, two enums of the same module with the variant, or, where no module of the program"
    "'s own has it, two imported enums with it). Provenance: the candidate declarations. Repair: qualify "
    "the name.\n- `diag.name-not-visible` — Summary: this item is private to its module. Phase: static. "
    "Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Not-Visible]`; `rule.module.visibility` `[Field-Not-Visible]` "
    "(a field named by `e.f`, a struct literal, or a destructuring). Required: `visible(M', name, M)`. Ob"
    "served: private. Provenance: the declaration's `export` marker vs. the use site's module. Repair: ma"
    "rk `export` or move the reference.\n- `diag.no-main` — Summary: the program has no `main` it can st"
    "art from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.program` `[Program-No-Main]`. Invariant: none. Required: exa"
    "ctly one non-generic, non-`extern` `main` at the root module, with no parameters, returning `void` o"
    "r `u8`. Observed: none there (a `main` inside a module is the ordinary item `m::main`), or one with "
    "parameters, another return type, type parameters, or `extern`. Provenance: the root module's items. "
    "Repair: declare `fn main()` or `fn main() : u8` at the root (arguments come from `arg`, `spec/21` §"
    "2c), or run the file that has one — a file-backed module's body is not a program (`spec/17` §5). "
    "Location: the root `main`, if there is one; otherwise the program as a whole.\n- `diag.const-not-cons"
    "tant` — Summary: a constant's value must be known before the program runs. Phase: static. Rule: `r"
    "ule.module.const` `[Const-Not-Constant]`, `[Const-Cycle]`, `[Const-Local-Not-Constant]` (`spec/17` §"
    "1a). Invariant: none. Required: a `const`'s type is not a resource, its initializer is a constant ex"
    "pression (literals, operators, other constants, struct, array and variant literals of constant expre"
    "ssions and their fields and elements, a function's name, the pure intrinsics listed there), and no c"
    "onstant depends on itself; a local constant's initializer names no local variable and no type parame"
    "ter of its function. Observed: one of these fails. Provenance: the `const` declaration. Repair: use "
    "only constants in the initializer (a local variable is not one, even when set from a literal: declar"
    "e it `const` too), compute the value in a function instead, or break the cycle. Location: the `const"
    "`.\n- `diag.format-invalid` — Summary: this format string is not valid. Phase: static. Rule: `rule."
    "stdlib.format` `[Format-Invalid]` (`spec/21` §2f). Invariant: none. Required: the format of `printf"
    "`, `sprintf`, `eprintf` or `String::appendf` is a string literal whose every `%` begins a specifier "
    "`%[flags][width][.precision]conversion` with a conversion of `d i u x X o b f F e E g G s v` (or is "
    "`%%`), and flags the conversion takes. Observed: a format that is not a literal, a `%` at the end, a"
    "n unknown conversion, a flag the conversion does not take (`%#d`, `%0s`, `%+x`, `%05v`), a precision"
    " on `%v`, or a width or precision above 4096. Provenance: the call. Repair: fix the specifier; write"
    " `%%` for a `%`. Location: the call.\n- `diag.module-file-not-found` — Summary: the module's file c"
    "annot be read. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[Module-File-Missing]`. Invariant: none. Req"
    "uired: the declaration's path, resolved against the declaring file's directory, names a readable fil"
    "e. Observed: it names none. Provenance: the declaration's path and the directory it was resolved aga"
    "inst. Repair: fix the path or create the file. Location: the `module` declaration.\n- `diag.module-cy"
    "cle` — Summary: these module files contain each other. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[M"
    "odule-File-Cycle]`. Invariant: none. Required: no file's body contains, directly or through further "
    "file-backed declarations, itself. Observed: a cycle `F → … → F`. Provenance: each declaration "
    "on the cycle. Repair: break the cycle — move the shared items into a third file both name. Locatio"
    "n: the declaration that closes the cycle.\n- `diag.module-file-duplicate` — Summary: this file is a"
    "lready declared as a module. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[Module-File-Duplicate]`. Inva"
    "riant: none. Required: each file is named by at most one declaration in the program. Observed: two. "
    "Provenance: both declarations. Repair: declare the module once and reach it by qualified path or `im"
    "port`. Location: the second declaration.\n- `diag.duplicate-local` — Summary: this name is already "
    "declared in this block. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.value-object.binding-form` `[Binding-Form-Redecla"
    "red]` (D-0131). Invariant: none. Required: each name is declared at most once in a declaration regio"
    "n — a block's statements with the parameters, loop names or pattern binder governing it. Observed:"
    " a second declaration (a local variable, a destructured binder, a local constant, a parameter, or a "
    "loop's or pattern's name). Provenance: both declarations (the message says how far above the first o"
    "ne is). Repair: assign to the existing variable (`x = …`, after a `drop` for a live resource), or "
    "choose another name, as when the type changes; a nested block may shadow. Location: the second decla"
    "ration.\n- `diag.duplicate-item` — Summary: this name is already declared in this module. Phase: st"
    "atic. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Item-Duplicate]`. Invariant: none. Required: each qualified name"
    " — `M::name` for a `fn`, `extern fn`, `struct`, `enum` or `module`, `M::T::name` for an associated"
    " function, `M::E::V` for an enum variant — is added by at most one declaration. Observed: two. Pro"
    "venance: both declarations. Repair: rename one, or move it into a module. Location: the second decla"
    "ration.\n- `diag.foreign-associated-fn` — Summary: an associated function must be declared beside i"
    "ts type. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Assoc-Fn-Foreign-Type]`. Invariant: none. Requ"
    "ired: `fn T::name` is declared in the module that declares the struct or enum `T`. Observed: `T` is "
    "declared elsewhere (for example `std`'s `Vec`) or not at all. Provenance: the declaration and `T`'s "
    "module. Repair: declare an ordinary function, or move the declaration into `T`'s module. Location: t"
    "he declaration.\n- `diag.unittest-name` — Summary: this test's name cannot be used. Phase: static. "
    "Rule: `rule.module.unittest` `[Unittest-Name]` (`spec/17` §6, D-0230). Invariant: none. Required: a"
    " `unittest`'s name, when it has one, is not empty, holds no control character, and is not the name o"
    "f another test of the same module. Observed: an empty name, a control character, or a second test of"
    " the module with that name. Provenance: the test and, for a repeated name, the first test with it. R"
    "epair: name each test of a module differently, say what it checks, or leave the name out. Location: "
    "the name.\n- `diag.type-mismatch` — Summary: the types do not match. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.typ"
    "e.typing` (any `[T-*]` premise failing), `[T-Convert]`, `[T-Alt]`, `[Limits-Not-Number]`, `[Print-No"
    "t-Printable]`, `[Append-Not-Printable]`, `[Parse-Not-Numeric]`, `[Format-Arg-Mismatch]`, `[Key-Not-H"
    "ashable]`, `[Foreach-Not-Iterable]`, `[Foreach-Range-Ill-Typed]`, `[Let-Destructure-Fields]`, `[Arra"
    "y-Repeat-Not-Plain]`. Required: the operand types the rule names. Observed: a different type. Proven"
    "ance: each operand's declaration or synthesis site. Repair: convert explicitly (`rule.arith.convert`"
    ") or fix the types.\n- `diag.unbounded-type-parameter` — Summary: the type parameter's bound does n"
    "ot allow this. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.type.kind`, `rule.type.bound` `[Bound-Missing]`. Required:"
    " only the permitted uses of `T`, and the operators its bound provides. Observed: an operator its bou"
    "nd (if any) does not provide, field access, or call on `T`. Provenance: the generic declaration. Rep"
    "air: give `T` the bound the operator needs (`<T: ordered>`, D-0090), or pass the operation in as a `"
    "fn` parameter.\n- `diag.cannot-infer-type-parameter` — Summary: a type argument cannot be inferred "
    "here. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.generic-call` `[Generic-Call-Uninferable]`, `rule.arith.limits` "
    "`[Limits-Uninferable]`. Required: every type parameter determined by an argument or the expected typ"
    "e. Observed: one is not. Provenance: the argument list and enclosing annotation, both lacking it. Re"
    "pair: `name<τ>(…)` or annotate the declaration. Related: `ex.generic-box`.\n- `diag.instantiation-"
    "unbounded` — Summary: a generic function's instantiations do not end. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.f"
    "n.generic-call` `[Generic-Instantiation-Unbounded]`. Required: a finite set of instantiations, each "
    "type argument nested at most 64 deep, at most 100,000 in all. Observed: an instantiation at a type a"
    "rgument nested deeper (a function calling itself at a larger type: `f<T>` calling `f<Box<T>>`), or m"
    "ore instantiations. Provenance: the generic function's declaration. Repair: pass the larger value as"
    " a type the function already has (a `Vec`, a `Box` of one fixed type), or split the function.\n- `dia"
    "g.break-outside-loop`, `diag.return-outside-fn` — Summary: `break`, `continue` or `return` has not"
    "hing to leave here. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.control.while` / `rule.fn.return`. Required: lexicall"
    "y inside a `while` / function body. Repair: move the statement.\n- `diag.capture-list-mismatch` — S"
    "ummary: the capture list does not match the names the closure uses. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.cl"
    "osure` `[Closure-Capture-List-Rejected]`. Invariant: none (a well-formedness check on the closure li"
    "teral, not a safety invariant). Required: the written capture list, as a set, equals the closure bod"
    "y's free variables. Observed: a name missing from the list, an extra name not used in the body, or b"
    "oth. Provenance: the closure literal's `[...]` vs. a syntactic scan of its body. Repair: add the mis"
    "sing name(s) or remove the unused one(s); the list documents an already-derived fact, it cannot sele"
    "ct a different capture set. Related: `ex.closure-capture`.\n\n## Validity of access paths\n\n- `diag.sta"
    "le-binding` — Summary: this value is no longer valid. Phase: both. Rule: `[Binding-Lookup-Stale]`,"
    " `[Read-Stale]`, `[Write-Stale]`, `[Borrow-Stale]`, `[Field-Access-Stale]`, `[Destroy-Stale]`, `[Fn-"
    "Value-Empty-Call]`. Invariant: `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: `temporally-valid(a)`. Observed: f"
    "alse. Provenance: the invalidating event (object end at frame exit, last holder ended, statement end"
    ", transfer, relocation, buffer release, a `fn` value's closure moved out) vs. this use. Repair: use "
    "the current holder after a move, or give the binding a new value first (`x = e`, `spec/11` `[Assign-"
    "Reestablish]`); do not keep a reference past its referent's or its holder's scope; re-index after a "
    "`Vec` reallocation. Related: `ex.use-after-move`, `ex.double-destroy`.\n- `diag.use-of-uninitialized`"
    " — Summary: this is used before it has a value. Phase: static (`rule.init.definite-assignment`, re"
    "jects on unknown); dynamic guard `[Read-Uninitialized]`, `[Write-Partial-Init]`. Invariant: `inv.ini"
    "tialization-validity`. Required: `init = valid` (a whole-object write on every path; no field write "
    "into an uninitialized aggregate). Observed: a path without a write, or a projection write before the"
    " whole. Provenance: the CFG path from block entry. Repair: initialize on every path; initialize aggr"
    "egates whole. Related: `ex.definite-assignment`.\n- `diag.reference-escapes-scope` — Summary: this "
    "reference would outlive what it refers to. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.temporal.ref-escape`, `rule.te"
    "mporal.elision`. Invariant: `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: no use of the reference outside its r"
    "eferent's block. Observed: stored into an enclosing block's binding or returned. Provenance: `refere"
    "nt-block` vs. the escaping store. Repair: return an owned value, or restructure. Related: `ex.refere"
    "nce-escape`.\n- `diag.lifetime-elision-ambiguous` — Summary: it is not clear which parameter the re"
    "turned reference comes from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.temporal.elision` `[Call-Multi-Ref-Return-Re"
    "jected]`. Required: exactly one reference parameter when returning a reference. Observed: zero or se"
    "veral. Provenance: the signature. Repair: one reference parameter, or return owned; `feat.explicit-l"
    "ifetime-parameters` is the open general case. Related: `ex.lifetime-elision`.\n\n## Aliasing\n\n- `diag."
    "aliasing-conflict` — Summary: this access conflicts with a live reference. Phase: both. Rule: `[Bo"
    "rrow-Denied]`, `[Read-Conflict]`, `[Write-Conflict]`, `[Match-Conflict]`, `[Thread-Affine]` (D-0213:"
    " an exclusive path of another running thread), `[Thread-Lend]` (a second lend of a live lent path). "
    "Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: `¬clash(a, m)`. Observed: `w"
    "itness(a, m, Σ)` — a live non-ancestor path with overlapping target and incompatible mode. Proven"
    "ance: the witness's formation event (which borrow, in which thread) vs. this access. Repair: end the"
    " conflicting reference (let its holder go out of scope) before this access, or use `shared` on both "
    "sides. Related: `ex.borrow-conflict`, `ex.projection-conflict`.\n- `diag.borrow-exceeds-source` — S"
    "ummary: this reference would allow more than its source does. Phase: static; dynamic for `[Read-Fn-T"
    "hrough-Shared]`. Rule: `[Borrow-Exceeds-Source]`, `[T-Read-Through-Shared]` (an exclusive reference "
    "read through a shared one, where an exclusive one is expected), `[Read-Exclusive-Through-Shared]`, `"
    "[Match-Exclusive-Through-Shared]`, `[Read-Fn-Through-Shared]` (D-0218). Invariant: `inv.alias-validi"
    "ty`. Required: an exclusive borrow's source is exclusive; nothing reached through a shared reference"
    " is used as a writer. Observed: source mode `shared`; a copy holding an exclusive reference; a closu"
    "re with an exclusive capture. Provenance: the source reference's declared mode. Repair: take `ref<τ"
    ", exclusive>` where mutation is needed. Related: `ex.shared-is-read-only`.\n- `diag.write-through-sha"
    "red` — Summary: this writes through a shared reference. Phase: static. Rule: `[Write-Not-Exclusive"
    "]` (a place reached through a shared path, including through an exclusive reference it holds: `[Read"
    "-Ref-Through-Shared]`, D-0218). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`. Required: `mode(a) = exclusive`. Ob"
    "served: `shared`. Provenance: the path's mode at formation. Repair: as above. Related: `ex.shared-is"
    "-read-only`.\n- `diag.destroy-while-aliased` — Summary: this is destroyed while a reference to it i"
    "s live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destroy-Not-Solitary]`. Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.temporal-"
    "validity`. Required: `solitary(a)`. Observed: another live path (a reference, a guard). Provenance: "
    "that path's formation. Repair: let the reference's holder end first; release the guard. Related: `ex"
    ".destroy-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag.move-while-aliased` — Summary: this is moved while a reference t"
    "o it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Transfer-Aliased]`, `[Relocate-In-Aliased]`, `[Rawptr-M"
    "ove-In]`/`-Out]` premises. Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`. Required: no other live path on the move"
    "d object. Observed: one exists. Provenance: its formation. Repair: end the reference before moving. "
    "Related: `ex.move-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag.move-out-of-field` — Summary: a part of a live value ca"
    "nnot be moved out on its own. Phase: static. Rule: `[Store-Binding-Place-Transfer-Sub]`, `[Destroy-P"
    "rojection]`, `[Match-Move-Through-Ref]`, `[Let-Destructure-Destructor]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-au"
    "thority`. Required: a moved resource is a whole object. Observed: a field/element/payload of a live "
    "object, or a payload reached through a reference. Provenance: the projection. Repair: move the whole"
    " container, or take a reference to the field.\n- `diag.borrow-of-non-place`, `diag.borrow-of-temporar"
    "y` — Summary: only a place can be borrowed. Phase: static. Rule: `[Ref-Form-Not-Place]`, `[Ref-For"
    "m-Temporary]`; `[Simd-Lane]` (`spec/16` §3b, D-0254). Required: the operand of `&` is a place roote"
    "d in a binding, reference, or reclaim. Observed: a value or a temporary; a bit field; a lane of a `s"
    "imd`, or a range of them. Repair: bind it first; read or assign the lane, or borrow the whole vector"
    ".\n\n## Resource authority\n\n- `diag.no-destroy-authority` — Summary: this code no longer owns the va"
    "lue it destroys. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destroy-No-Authority]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. R"
    "equired: unconsumed authority in this thread. Observed: absent (moved to another thread) or consumed"
    ". Provenance: the consuming/transferring event. Repair: destroy in the owning thread, once. (A secon"
    "d `drop(x)` through the same binding reports `diag.stale-binding` first.) Related: `ex.double-destro"
    "y`.\n- `diag.transfer-without-authority` — Summary: this code no longer owns the value it hands on."
    " Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Transfer-Unauthorized]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`, `inv.t"
    "emporal-validity`. Required: a valid source holding authority. Observed: stale or unauthorized. Prov"
    "enance: the earlier move/destroy. Repair: move from the current holder. Related: `ex.use-after-move`"
    ".\n- `diag.overwrite-of-live-resource` — Summary: this overwrites a resource that has not been ende"
    "d. Phase: both. Rule: `[Write-Resource-Overwrite-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Re"
    "quired: the target holds no live resource, or its type is quiet (D-0194: then the write destroys it)"
    ". Observed: an outstanding obligation at the target. Provenance: the establishing/moving event that "
    "put it there. Repair: `overwrite(&mut place, v)` to put `v` there and destroy the old value (D-0080)"
    ", `replace(&mut place, v)` to keep the old value, or `drop` the old value first. Related: `ex.no-sil"
    "ent-resource-overwrite`.\n- `diag.read-of-resource` — Summary: a resource cannot be copied by readi"
    "ng it. Phase: static. Rule: `[Read-Resource-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Require"
    "d: `¬is-resource(type(a))` in value position. Observed: resource. Provenance: the type declaration."
    " Repair: move it, or take a reference. Related: `ex.no-copy-of-resource`.\n- `diag.destructor-on-plai"
    "n-type` — Summary: only a resource can have a destructor. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/07` §1 (D-00"
    "75). Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: a type with a destructor is a resource in every "
    "instantiation. Observed: `T::drop` declared for a type that is not one. Provenance: the destructor's"
    " declaration. Repair: declare the type `resource struct T` (or `resource enum T`).\n- `diag.bad-destr"
    "uctor-signature`, `diag.direct-destructor-call` — Summary: a destructor must be `T::drop(ref<T, ex"
    "clusive> self)`, called only by `drop`. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/07` §1. Required: `T::drop(ref<T"
    ", exclusive> self)`, invoked only by `[Destroy]`. Repair: fix the signature; use `drop(x)`.\n\n## Arit"
    "hmetic\n\n- `diag.arith-overflow` — Summary: arithmetic overflow. Phase: both. Rule: `[Arith-Checked"
    "-Overflow]`, `[Neg-Overflow]`. Invariant: `inv.arith.range-validity`. Required: `r ∈ represented-d"
    "omain(τ)`. Observed: outside. Provenance: the operand values at this expression. Repair: widen, or "
    "use `wrapping_`/`saturating_`/`checked_`. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`, `ex.negation`.\n- `diag.d"
    "iv-by-zero` — Summary: division by zero. Phase: both. Rule: `[Div-By-Zero]`. Required: `v2 ≠ 0`."
    " Repair: test first, or `checked_div`. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`.\n- `diag.div-overflow` — S"
    "ummary: division overflow: the minimum divided by -1. Phase: both. Rule: `[Div-Overflow]`. Required:"
    " `¬(v1 = min(τ) ∧ v2 = -1)`. Repair: `checked_div` or widen. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`.\n-"
    " `diag.shift-amount-out-of-range` — Summary: shift amount out of range for the type. Phase: both. "
    "Rule: `[Shift-Amount-Invalid]`. Required: `0 ≤ n < bitwidth(τ)`. Repair: mask the amount.\n- `diag"
    ".narrowing-overflow` — Summary: the value does not fit the narrower type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Nar"
    "row-Overflow]`, `[Float-To-Int-Invalid]`, `[Bitfield-Overflow]` (`spec/16` §2a, D-0118). Required: "
    "`v ∈ represented-domain(τ')`. Repair: `narrow_wrapping`, or widen the target.\n- `diag.literal-out"
    "-of-range` — Summary: this literal does not fit its type. Phase: static. Rule: `[Literal-Out-Of-Ra"
    "nge]`. Required: `val(L) ∈ represented-domain(τ)`; for a float literal, that it does not round be"
    "yond `τ`'s largest finite magnitude. Provenance: the literal vs. its determined type. Repair: fix t"
    "he literal or annotation.\n\n## Aggregates\n\n- `diag.recursive-type` — Summary: this type contains it"
    "self. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.agg.layout` `[Type-Recursive]` (`spec/16` §1). Invariant: none. Re"
    "quired: no struct or enum contains itself by value. Observed: a chain of fields, payloads, array ele"
    "ments or `mutex` values leading back to the type, with no pointer on the way. Provenance: the type's"
    " declaration. Repair: put the recursive part behind a `Box<T>` (one owner), an `Rc<T>` (shared) or a"
    " `Vec<T>` (many). Location: the declaration.\n- `diag.static-assert-failed` — Summary: static asser"
    "tion failed. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static-assert` `[Static-Assert-Failed]` (`spec/17` §"
    "1). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `static_assert` is `true`. Observed: `false`, for th"
    "e program as written or for one instantiation of a generic function (the message given, if any, is s"
    "hown, formatted with its arguments' values). Provenance: the assertion and the constants and types i"
    "t names. Repair: fix what the assertion guards, or the assertion. Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.s"
    "tatic-assert-not-constant` — Summary: a static assertion's condition must be known before the prog"
    "ram runs. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static-assert` `[Static-Assert-Not-Constant]` (`spec/17`"
    " §1b). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `static_assert` is a `bool` constant expression "
    "— literals, constants (module or local), operators, `sizeof`, `alignof`, the limits and the conver"
    "sions — so that it can be computed before the program runs. Observed: the condition (or an argumen"
    "t of its message) names a local variable or parameter, calls a function or reads a container, or the"
    " condition is not a `bool`. Provenance: the condition. Repair: for a condition that is only known wh"
    "en the program runs, use `assert` (`spec/18` §1a); to check a value before the program runs, name i"
    "t with `const` (a local `const` works: `const u8 D = B + 1;`). Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.not-"
    "char-boundary` — Summary: this bound falls inside a character. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib."
    "stringview` `[View-Boundary]` (`spec/21` §2h). Invariant: `inv.string.utf8-validity`. Required: bot"
    "h bounds of a `StringView` fall at the start of a character or at the end of the text. Observed: a b"
    "ound inside a character's UTF-8 encoding. Provenance: the view's bounds. Repair: move the bound to a"
    " character's start (a byte that is not `0b10xxxxxx`), for example by searching with `StringView::fin"
    "d`. Location: the view.\n- `diag.invalid-datetime` — Summary: this date and time do not exist. Phas"
    "e: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.time` `[Invalid-DateTime]` (`spec/21` §2j, D-0140). Invariant: none."
    " Required: the `DateTime` names a moment of the proleptic Gregorian calendar (a month 1 to 12, a day"
    " within its month, an hour below 24, a minute and a second below 60) at most `i64` seconds from 1970"
    ". Observed: a field out of range, or a year too far from 1970. Provenance: the `DateTime`, written a"
    "s a struct literal or with its fields changed. Repair: make it with `DateTime::new`, which returns `"
    "None` for such fields, or with `DateTime::from_unix`/`from_iso`. Location: the call of `DateTime::to"
    "_unix` (or `weekday`).\n- `diag.entropy-unavailable` — Summary: the operating system gave no secure"
    " random bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §0 `[Os-Random]` (D-0142). Invariant: none. Required"
    ": the operating system gives bytes from its cryptographically secure source. Observed: it has none, "
    "or refused (on Linux, no `getrandom` and no readable `/dev/urandom`, as in a bare container). Proven"
    "ance: the call. Repair: run where the system provides secure randomness; never substitute a clock or"
    " a fixed seed for keys. Location: the call of `os_random_bytes`, `os_random_u64` or `Rng::from_os`.\n"
    "- `diag.hkdf-length` — Summary: HKDF cannot produce more than 8160 bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `s"
    "pec/21` §2m `[Hkdf]` (D-0152). Invariant: none. Required: `hkdf_expand`'s `len` is at most 8160, 25"
    "5 blocks of 32 bytes (RFC 5869's bound). Observed: a larger `len`. Provenance: the call. Repair: der"
    "ive at most 8160 bytes from one pseudorandom key; derive more keys with different `info`. Location: "
    "the call of `hkdf_expand` or `hkdf_sha256`.\n- `diag.crypto-length` — Summary: a key, nonce or dige"
    "st of the wrong length. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Crypto-Length]` (D-0153, D-0154, D-01"
    "65, D-0167, D-0168, D-0169, D-0170). Invariant: none. Required: a ChaCha20 or AEAD key of 32 bytes a"
    "nd a nonce of 12, an AES key of 16, 24 or 32 bytes and an AES-GCM nonce of 12 (D-0165), an X25519, P"
    "-256 or Ed25519 private key of 32 bytes and a P-384 private key of 48, a Poly1305 key of 32 bytes, a"
    " ChaCha20 message that fits in the 2^32 blocks after its starting counter, a BLAKE2b digest of 1 to "
    "64 bytes under a key of at most 64, an RSA digest of its hash's length and a modulus long enough for"
    " the signature encoding, and an RSA key size of 1024 to 8192 bits in a multiple of 64. Observed: ano"
    "ther length. Provenance: the call. Repair: pass keys and nonces of the algorithm's sizes (a key from"
    " `hkdf_expand` with `len` 32, a nonce of 12 bytes, a digest from `hash` of the `HashKind` named). Lo"
    "cation: the call into `std::crypto`.\n- `diag.kdf-parameters` — Summary: the key-derivation paramet"
    "ers are out of range. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Kdf-Parameters]` (D-0170). Invariant: n"
    "one. Required: `pbkdf2` runs at least one iteration; `argon2id` (and a PHC string `verify_password` "
    "reads, which is false instead) has at least one pass, 1 to 255 lanes, at least 8 KiB of memory per l"
    "ane, a salt of at least 8 bytes and a result of at least 4 bytes (RFC 9106 §3.1). Observed: a param"
    "eter outside those bounds. Provenance: the call. Repair: pass the parameters the standard allows; `h"
    "ash_password` chooses them itself. Location: the call of `pbkdf2` or `argon2id`.\n- `diag.not-ascii` "
    "— Summary: this byte is not ASCII. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.text` `[Push-Ascii-Not-Ascii"
    "]` (`spec/21` §2d). Invariant: `inv.string.utf8-validity`. Required: the byte given to `String::pus"
    "h_ascii` is below 128. Observed: a byte of 128 or more, which is not UTF-8 on its own. Provenance: t"
    "he call. Repair: build bytes in a `Vec<u8>` and check them with `String::from_utf8`. Location: the c"
    "all.\n- `diag.index-out-of-bounds` — Summary: index out of bounds. Phase: both. Rule: `[Index-Out-O"
    "f-Bounds]`, `[Slice-Out-Of-Bounds]` (`spec/16` §3a), `spec/21` §1 `fault`, `[Str-Byte-Out-Of-Bound"
    "s]` (`spec/21` §2a), `arg`'s `fault` (`spec/21` §2c). Invariant: `inv.spatial-validity`. Required:"
    " `0 ≤ n < N` / `i < len` / `i < str_len(s)` / `i < arg_count()`. Observed: violated. Provenance: t"
    "he index value vs. the fixed `N`, current `len`, the `str`'s byte count, or the number of arguments."
    " Repair: check first, or use `pop`/`checked` accessors. Related: `ex.bounds-check`, `ex.str-literal`"
    ".\n- `diag.non-exhaustive-match` — Summary: this `match` does not cover every value. Phase: static."
    " Rule: `[Match-Non-Exhaustive]`. Required: the arms together match every value (every variant, at ev"
    "ery level a pattern descends to, or `_`). Observed: a pattern no arm matches, given as the message. "
    "Provenance: the enum declarations vs. the arms. Repair: add an arm for the pattern named, or a `_` a"
    "rm. Related: `ex.exhaustive-match`.\n- `diag.unreachable-arm` — Summary: this arm can never be reac"
    "hed. Phase: static. Rule: `[Match-Unreachable]`. Required: each arm matches some value no earlier ar"
    "m matches (arms are tried in order). Observed: an arm every value of which an earlier arm takes. Pro"
    "venance: the arm vs. the earlier arms. Repair: remove the arm, or move it before the arm that takes "
    "its values.\n\n## Failure, concurrency, trust\n\n- `diag.propagate-outside-fallible-context` — Summary"
    ": `?` cannot be used in this function. Phase: static. Rule: `[Propagate-Err-Mismatch]`, `[Propagate-"
    "Option-Mismatch]` (D-0130). Required: the function returns `Result<_, E>` with matching `E` (for a `"
    "Result` operand), or an `Option` (for an `Option` operand). Provenance: the declared return type vs."
    " the `?` site. Repair: change the return type, `Result::map_err`, `Option::ok_or(o, e)?` (an `Option"
    "` in a `Result`-returning function), or `match`.\n- `diag.spawn-borrow-closure` — Summary: a spawne"
    "d thread needs a `move` closure. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.conc.spawn`. Required: a `fn` value or `"
    "move` closure. Repair: add `move`.\n- `diag.mutex-reentrant-lock` — Summary: this thread already ho"
    "lds the lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `[Lock-Reentrant]`. Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Requi"
    "red: the thread does not already hold the lock. Provenance: the live guard. Repair: release the guar"
    "d first.\n- `diag.trusted-outside-unsafe` — Summary: this needs an `unsafe` block. Phase: static. R"
    "ule: `[Unsafe-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.trust-transition`. Required: every trusted construct insid"
    "e `unsafe { }`. Provenance: the construct vs. the nearest enclosing `unsafe`. Repair: wrap in `unsaf"
    "e` after verifying the asserted property. Related: `ex.unsafe-required`.\n- `diag.extern-non-ffi-type"
    "` — Summary: this type cannot cross into C. Phase: static. Rule: `[Extern-Non-Ffi-Type]`. Required"
    ": `FfiType` parameters and result: integers, `f32`, `f64`, `bool`, `void` (a result), `rawptr<τ>`, "
    "and plain structs of those (`ffi-struct`, D-0252). Observed: the first type that is none of these, n"
    "amed through the field path that reaches it. Repair: pass `rawptr`/scalars, or a struct without reso"
    "urces, enums or bitstructs.\n- `diag.null-pointer` — Summary: C's `NULL` where text was expected. P"
    "hase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.ffi` `[From-C-Null]` (`spec/21` §3f, D-0252). Invariant: none. Re"
    "quired: the `rawptr<u8>` given to `String::from_c` or `Vec::from_c_bytes` is not `null_rawptr<u8>()`"
    ". Observed: address 0. Provenance: the C function that returned it. Repair: test with `is_null` firs"
    "t; C functions return `NULL` for \"none\". Location: the call.\n- `diag.assert-failed` — Summary: ass"
    "ertion failed. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.fail.assert` `[Assert-Fail]` (`spec/18` §1a). Invariant:"
    " none. Required: the condition of `assert` is `true`. Observed: `false` (the message the program gav"
    "e, if any, formatted, is shown after the location). Provenance: the call. Repair: the program's own "
    "condition names what was assumed; find why it did not hold. Location: the call.\n- `diag.channel-zero"
    "-capacity` — Summary: a channel needs a capacity of at least 1. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.c"
    "hannel` `[Channel-Zero-Capacity]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: none. Required: the capacity given to "
    "`Channel::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call. Repair: give the number of values t"
    "he channel may hold; 1 for a hand-over. Location: the call.\n- `diag.barrier-zero-parties` — Summar"
    "y: a barrier needs at least one party. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.waiting` `[Barrier-Zero-Pa"
    "rties]` (`spec/21` §3c‴). Invariant: none. Required: the number of parties given to `Barrier::new"
    "` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call. Repair: give the number of threads that meet at "
    "the barrier. Location: the call.\n- `diag.channel-deadlock` — Summary: the only running thread wait"
    "s on a channel nothing else can change. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.channel` `[Channel-Deadlock"
    "]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: none. Required: while `Channel::send` or `Channel::recv` waits, anoth"
    "er thread exists that could change the channel. Observed: the program's only running thread waits on"
    " a full or empty channel that is not closed. Provenance: the call. Repair: send or receive from anot"
    "her thread, or `close` the channel before receiving the last value. Location: the call.\n- `diag.thre"
    "ad-cancelled` — Summary: this thread was cancelled. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.cancel` `[Can"
    "cel]` (`spec/19` §1, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the thread was not asked to stop while it "
    "waits. Observed: `cancel` was called on its handle; it was waiting (a join, a lock, a channel, sleep"
    "ing, a socket) or began to. Provenance: the `cancel` call. Repair: none is needed when the stop was "
    "meant: the thread's failure is contained, and its joiner or handle sees it; to let a thread finish, "
    "do not cancel it. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.mutex-poisoned` — Summary: a thread failed while hol"
    "ding this lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.lock` `[Lock-Poisoned]` (`spec/19` §2, D-0204). In"
    "variant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: the mutex was not held by a thread whose fault was co"
    "ntained. Observed: such a thread held it when it failed, so its interior may be half-changed. Proven"
    "ance: the failed thread's fault. Repair: find that fault (`try_join` gives it); keep a lock's block "
    "short, so that little can fail inside it. Location: the `lock`.\n- `diag.deadlock` — Summary: these"
    " threads would wait for each other forever. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.guarantee` `[Deadlock]`"
    " (`spec/19` §4, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the wait can end. Observed: waiting would close"
    " a cycle of threads waiting to join or lock each other's, or every thread waits on another, a mutex,"
    " a channel or an atomic (`Atomic::wait`, D-0253), and none on the clock or outside the program. Prov"
    "enance: the waits. Repair: take locks in one order; send before waiting to receive; store and notify"
    " before waiting on an atomic another thread waits to see change; join a thread only after giving it "
    "what it waits for. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.result-discarded` — Summary: a `Result` is discarde"
    "d. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/13` §3 `[Stmt-Result-Discarded]` (D-0099). Invariant: none. Required:"
    " a statement's value that is a `Result` is used — propagated with `?`, matched, bound, passed or r"
    "eturned. Observed: an expression statement (or a block-like statement) whose value is a `Result`, di"
    "scarded. Provenance: the statement. Repair: handle the error (`?`, `match`), or discard the value on"
    " purpose with `_ = e;`.\n- `diag.stack-exhausted` — Summary: calls nested too deeply for the stack."
    " Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/15` §3 `[Call-Stack-Exhausted]` (D-0077). Invariant: none (an implemen"
    "tation limit). Required: the implementation can give the call a frame. Observed: calls nested deeper"
    " than the stack the implementation provides. Provenance: the call. Repair: recurse less deeply (a lo"
    "op, an explicit stack in a `Vec`).\n- `diag.unwrap-failed` — Summary: nothing to unwrap: `None` or "
    "`Err`. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1 `Option::unwrap`, `Option::expect`, `Result::unwrap`, `Re"
    "sult::expect` (D-0082). Invariant: none. Required: the `Option` is `Some`, the `Result` is `Ok`. Obs"
    "erved: `None` or `Err` (`expect`'s message, or which call it was, is shown after the location). Prov"
    "enance: the call. Repair: match on the value, or give a default with `unwrap_or`, where its absence "
    "is possible. Location: the call.\n- `diag.alloc-failure` — Summary: memory could not be allocated. "
    "Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1/§3 `fault(alloc_failure)` after `allocate` returns `Err`. Requi"
    "red: allocation succeeded. Provenance: the `allocate` call. Repair: none at the language level; call"
    "ers needing recovery call `allocate` themselves.\n\n## Change Log\n\n- 1.61.0 — `CHG-0357`: `diag.inst"
    "antiation-unbounded`.\n- 1.60.0 — `CHG-0323` (D-0260): `diag.barrier-zero-parties`.\n- 1.59.0 — `C"
    "HG-0320` (D-0258): `diag.write-through-shared` also for `&mut` of a static; `diag.read-of-resource` "
    "for a static read or moved whole; `diag.type-mismatch` and `diag.literal-out-of-range` for an ill-fo"
    "rmed static; `diag.borrow-of-non-place` for `&mut` of a constant.\n- 1.58.0 — `CHG-0319` (D-0257): "
    "`diag.extern-non-ffi-type` also from `[Extern-Entry]` (an `extern fn` with a body); `diag.duplicate-"
    "item` also for a C name two entry points share or the runtime reserves; `diag.trusted-outside-unsafe"
    "` also from `Vec::from_raw` and `copy_to_raw`.\n- 1.57.0 — `CHG-0312` (D-0254): `diag.borrow-of-non"
    "-place` names a `simd`'s lane.\n- 1.56.0 — `CHG-0311` (D-0253): `diag.deadlock` covers a wait on an"
    " atomic.\n- 1.55.0 — `CHG-0309`, `CHG-0310` (D-0252): `diag.extern-non-ffi-type` admits plain struc"
    "ts; `diag.null-pointer`.\n- 1.54.0 — `CHG-0274` (D-0230): `diag.unittest-name`.\n- 1.53.0 — `CHG-0"
    "271` (D-0228): every entry has a **Summary**; a location has a column; \"How a diagnostic\n  is shown\""
